PREFIX: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-5
TITLE: Functional 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall jump to execution of the HVPS interface application
if and only if the existing application code at startup is valid. The application code is valid if the
programmed CRC value matches the application firmware loaded in flash memory.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory, but partway through, terminate the PC utility.
4. Power cycle the system.
5. Load a treatment plan.
6. Run the loaded treatment.
7. While keeping power on, load the application firmware once more through to completion from the flash memory.
8. Power cycle the system.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the system is off.
4. Verify system starts up successfully.
5. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
6. Verify the treatment plan cannot be executed.
7. Verify the application is loaded successfully.
8. Verify the system powered up successfully and the loaded treatment can now be performed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-6
TITLE: Functional 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall write application data provided by the PC through
application-relative page index 180.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A bootloader-compatible application image contains known, non-erased data at application-relative
  page index 180.
* A flash inspection tool is available to read the programmed application memory.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load the prepared application firmware image.
4. Record the utility log for the write to application-relative page index 180.
5. Read back application-relative page index 180 with the flash inspection tool.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the bootloader utility completes the application load without rejecting page index 180.
4. Verify the utility log reports that page index 180 was written successfully.
5. Verify the read-back data at page index 180 matches the prepared application image.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-7
TITLE: Functional 3 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash
memory, corresponding to the application firmware programming area.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start in bootloader mode.
* The application programming area contains known, non-erased marker data in its first page and at
  application-relative page index 180.
* A protocol-compatible tool can send an erase command and inspect MCU flash memory.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power in bootloader mode.
2. Use the protocol-compatible tool to send an erase command.
3. Record the bootloader response.
4. Read back the marker locations in the first application page and at application-relative page
   index 180.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully in bootloader mode.
2. Verify the bootloader reports that the erase completed.
3. Verify the erase response is received before inspecting flash.
4. Verify both marker locations contain the erased flash value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-8
TITLE: PC Communication - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to respond to a ping command from the PC,
indicating that the system is in bootloader mode.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory.
4. Record the utility log to ensure application enters bootloader mode.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the new firmware application is loaded successfully.
4. Verify application enters bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
  ROLE: Verifies

